      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 5545414368755638688, guid: 11889ddad84efa74cb6476a97ba23853, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Name
      value: StoryUICanvas
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7601046077032374988, guid: 11889ddad84efa74cb6476a97ba23853, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "The Monkey and the Turtle\\n\\nOne day, a Monkey met a Turtle on the
        road and asked, \"Where are you going?\"\\n\\n\"I am going to find something
        to eat, for I have had no food for three whole days,\" said the Turtle.\\n\\n\"I,
        too, am hungry,\" said the Monkey, \"and since we are both hungry, let us
        go together and hunt food for our stomach's sake.\"\\n\\nThey soon became
        good friends and chatted along the way, so that the time passed quickly.
        Before they had gone far, the Monkey saw a large bunch of yellow bananas
        on a tree at a distance.\\n\\n\"Oh, what a good sight that is!\" he cried.
        \"Don't you see the bananas hanging on that banana tree?\u201D He pointed
        with his first finger toward the tree, \u201CThey are fine! I can taste them
        already.\"\\n\\nBut the Turtle was short-sighted and could not see them.
        After a while, they came near the tree, and then he finally saw them. The
        two friends were very glad. The mere sight of the ripe, yellow fruit made
        them hungrier.\\n\\nBut the Turtle could not climb the tree, so he agreed
        that the Monkey should go up alone and throw some of the fruit down to him.\\n\\nThe
        Monkey was up in a flash and, seating himself comfortably, he began to eat
        the ripest of the fruit, and forgot to drop any down to the Turtle waiting
        below.\\n\\nThe Turtle called for some, but the Monkey pretended not to hear.
        He ate even the peelings and refused to drop a bit to his friend, who was
        patiently begging under the tree.\\n\\nAt last, the Turtle became angry,
        very angry indeed. So, he thought he would take revenge.\\n\\nWhile the Monkey
        was having a good time filling his stomach, the Turtle gathered sharp, broken
        pieces of glass and stuck them, one by one, all around the banana tree. Then
        he hid himself under a coconut shell not far away.\\n\\nThe Monkey could
        not eat all the bananas, for there was enough to last a good-sized family
        for several days. He ate all that he could, and then he started coming down
        the tree with great difficulty.\\n\\nThe sharp glasses then cut the hand
        of the Monkey, wounding him. He had a hard time, and his hands were full
        of cuts in many places. The Turtle was satisfied with his revenge.\\n\\nBut
        now, the Monkey was very angry at the trick the Turtle had played on him.
        He began searching for the Turtle, planning to punish him. For a while, he
        could not find his former friend.\\n\\nTired and in pain, he sat down on
        a coconut shell nearby. His anger only grew stronger as he rested, thinking
        about what the Turtle had done.\\n\\nHe sat there for a long time, sore from
        his wounds and wondering where the Turtle could be. As he shifted his weight
        on the shell, the Turtle\u2014who was hiding inside\u2014made a small noise.\\n\\nThe
        Monkey heard it and looked around, confused. He couldn\u2019t tell where
        the sound had come from. At last, he lifted the shell\u2014and there was
        the Turtle!\\n\\n\u201CAh! So here you are!\u201D the Monkey shouted. \u201CSay
        your prayers. This is the end for you!\u201D\\n\\nHe grabbed the Turtle by
        the neck and carried him to the riverbank. There, he prepared to punish him.
        He built a big fire and brought out a mortar and pestle. He was deciding
        whether to burn the Turtle or grind him into pieces.\\n\\nWhen everything
        was ready, he asked the Turtle to choose how he wanted to die: in the fire
        or in the mortar. The Turtle begged for his life. But when he saw that the
        Monkey would not forgive him, he cried, \u201CPlease, do anything\u2014but
        don\u2019t throw me into the water!\u201D\\n\\nWhen the Monkey heard this,
        he thought it was the perfect punishment. He picked up the Turtle with his
        bleeding fingers and threw him as hard as he could into the river.\\n\\nTo
        the Monkey\u2019s surprise, the Turtle was delighted. He laughed and popped
        his head out of the water.\\n\\n\u201CThis is my home!\u201D the Turtle shouted.
        \u201CThe water is where I belong!\u201D\\n\\nHearing this, the Monkey became
        so angry that he lost control. He jumped into the river to catch the Turtle\u2014but
        he could not swim, and he drowned.\\n\\nSince that day, monkeys and turtles
        have been bitter enemies.\\n\\n- The End -"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
